WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.173 --> 00:00:02.373
- Well, well, well, well.
- Hi.

00:00:02.373 --> 00:00:04.380
- Well wait, I was-
- How are you?

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.180
- I'm great, but you're doing well!

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.008
- I am.
- So, congratulations.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.840
We need to start with a big congrats,

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:10.950
I don't know if everybody knows,

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:11.970
but last month you said that you'd

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.520
been undergoing cancer
treatment for a year,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.110
which I didn't know about,
so I don't know then

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:16.943
if many people knew about-

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:17.776
- 'Cause you're not supposed to know

00:00:17.776 --> 00:00:18.609
about it.
- Yeah, I was like, I don't

00:00:18.609 --> 00:00:19.442
think many people knew about-
- I kept it quiet.

00:00:19.442 --> 00:00:20.275
- You did!

00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:21.108
- Yes.

00:00:21.108 --> 00:00:23.700
- And you got the news that
you're now cancer-free, right?

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.533
- I am.
(audience cheering)

00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:25.366
Yeah.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.313
Thank you.

00:00:28.313 --> 00:00:29.820
- That's a hard thing to keep quiet!

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.470
- I...

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.340
Listen-

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.660
- [Kelly] Just physically,
while you're working.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.493
- Yeah, it is.

00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:35.940
It was hard.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.660
The thing was, I didn't
wanna say anything.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:44.250
I don't want pity, and
I don't have a publicist

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.267
that you release it and everybody says,

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.720
"Oh my God, Kelly."

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:49.553
I didn't want that.
- Yeah.

00:00:49.553 --> 00:00:50.653
- That happens.
- Yeah.

00:00:50.653 --> 00:00:51.810
- I just wanted to keep it quiet.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.400
My family knew.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.090
And then, as you can tell,
I'm a little self-conscious

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.690
about my appearance, but
that's from the treatments.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.000
And people were saying,
what's wrong with me?

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.440
What's wrong with me?

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.420
And so finally, I thank Fox

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.090
for allowing me the time to say

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:10.950
- Yeah.
- in November I was diagnosed

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.147
with bladder cancer.

00:01:12.147 --> 00:01:12.980
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.240
- And I went on this treatment at Baylor,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.930
I didn't mean Baylor, Yale Medical Center

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:22.860
up in New Haven,
Connecticut for six weeks.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.840
Then I came back and was diagnosed
weeks later, cancer-free.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.580
But I still do follow up treatments

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.440
which I still have to go back up for that.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.033
- Which are hard on your body.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:35.070
- You have no idea.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.450
I had no idea!

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.720
- Yeah.
- It's bladder cancer,

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.060
and then in March,

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.610
I'm getting ready to go to
Hawaii, and I'm all excited

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:47.460
I get a vacation after,
well, over two years.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.310
And I was having trouble with my neck,

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.257
and I go in, my wife says,

00:01:53.257 --> 00:01:54.750
"We need to get that checked."

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:58.170
And then they found a
tumor here. (chuckles)

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.720
So that's Merkel cell cancer.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.690
- Oh my God.
- It's a form of skin cancer.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.360
It's relatively rare.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.755
Had it not been for this, then
we wouldn't have found that.

00:02:08.755 --> 00:02:10.440
- Yeah, they didn't catch it.
- So they cut all that out,

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.590
and now my face is a
little, I'm self-conscious.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:15.690
My wife says, "You look fine."

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:16.680
But-
- Yeah, I gotta be honest

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:17.533
with you, it's just-
- But my-

00:02:17.533 --> 00:02:18.366
- If I had...
- Yeah, I didn't know.

00:02:18.366 --> 00:02:19.199
- But you know what Kelly?

00:02:19.199 --> 00:02:20.032
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- It's like,

00:02:20.032 --> 00:02:24.480
I'm so self-conscious of my face.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.040
One good thing about
it, though, I don't have

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.510
to shave, cause I have no hair

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:28.343
over here.
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:02:28.343 --> 00:02:32.730
So it's been a long battle.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.527
And then I went back to MD Anderson

00:02:34.527 --> 00:02:38.160
and got cancer-free here.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:38.993
- Jeez,
- So,

00:02:38.993 --> 00:02:40.320
what a blessing though.
- as we do this interview-

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.706
- Yeah.
(audience applauding)

00:02:41.706 --> 00:02:42.539
- But...

00:02:44.763 --> 00:02:49.763
It's like, "One cancer, wow!"

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.480
Two?
- Two, yeah.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.313
- Two is

00:02:52.313 --> 00:02:53.311
a little bit overwhelming.
- When it rains, it pours.

00:02:53.311 --> 00:02:54.210
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.460
- But I've always had a
great attitude about it.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.250
Never thought that it was,
I never, I don't know why.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.450
Maybe it's my faith.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.283
- Well, do you-

00:03:01.283 --> 00:03:03.007
